IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc22-joinder.l4 -- sections 589 to 596 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XX: joinder or severance of counts; joinder of accused in certain cases). Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING);
-- [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless). Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section.

§ `Section 589 -- Count for murder`

-- The BAR: JUST TRUE where the section bars joining the count to a count that charges murder.
-- src:12662 | 589 No count that charges an indictable offence other than murder shall be joined in an indictment to a count that charges murder unless
-- src:12663 | (a) the count that charges the offence other than murder arises out of the same transaction as a count that charges murder; or
-- src:12664 | (b) the accused signifies consent to the joinder of the counts.
@ref s 589 (src:12662-12664)
GIVEN `the count charges an indictable offence other than murder and is to be joined in an indictment to a count that charges murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the count that charges the offence other than murder arises out of the same transaction as a count that charges murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused signifies consent to the joinder of the counts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 589 the section bars joining the count to a count that charges murder` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the count charges an indictable offence other than murder and is to be joined in an indictment to a count that charges murder` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No count that charges an indictable offence other than murder shall be joined in an indictment to a count that charges murder"
        IF `the count that charges the offence other than murder arises out of the same transaction as a count that charges murder` OR `the accused signifies consent to the joinder of the counts` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be joined in an indictment to a count that charges murder unless (a) the count that charges the offence other than murder arises out of the same transaction" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 590 -- Offences may be charged in the alternative`

-- src:12666 | 590 (1) A count is not objectionable by reason only that
-- src:12667 | (a) it charges in the alternative several different matters, acts or omissions that are stated in the alternative in an enactment that describes as an indictable offence the matters, acts or omissions charged in the count; or
-- src:12668 | (b) it is double or multifarious.
@ref s 590(1) (src:12666-12668)
DECLARE `s 590(1) the ground of objection` IS ONE OF
    `s 590(1)(a) it charges in the alternative several different matters, acts or omissions that are stated in the alternative in an enactment that describes as an indictable offence the matters, acts or omissions charged in the count`
    `s 590(1)(b) it is double or multifarious`
    `s 590(1) some other ground`

-- src:12666 | 590 (1) A count is not objectionable by reason only that
-- src:12667 | (a) it charges in the alternative several different matters, acts or omissions that are stated in the alternative in an enactment that describes as an indictable offence the matters, acts or omissions charged in the count; or
-- src:12668 | (b) it is double or multifarious.
@ref s 590(1) (src:12666-12668)
GIVEN ground IS A `s 590(1) the ground of objection`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 590(1) the ground alone makes the count objectionable` MEANS
    IF ground EQUALS `s 590(1) some other ground`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A count is not objectionable by reason only that (a) ... or (b) it is double or multifarious"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A count is not objectionable by reason only that" [M-a]

-- src:12670 | (2) An accused may at any stage of his trial apply to the court to amend or to divide a count that
-- src:12671 | (a) charges in the alternative different matters, acts or omissions that are stated in the alternative in the enactment that describes the offence or declares that the matters, acts or omissions charged are an indictable offence, or
-- src:12672 | (b) is double or multifarious,
-- src:12673 | on the ground that, as framed, it embarrasses him in his defence.
@ref s 590(2) (src:12670-12673)
GIVEN `the application is made at a stage of the accused’s trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the count charges in the alternative different matters, acts or omissions stated in the alternative in the enactment, or is double or multifarious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground is that, as framed, the count embarrasses the accused in their defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 590(2) the accused may apply to the court to amend or to divide the count` MEANS
    IF `the application is made at a stage of the accused’s trial` AND `the count charges in the alternative different matters, acts or omissions stated in the alternative in the enactment, or is double or multifarious` AND `the ground is that, as framed, the count embarrasses the accused in their defence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused may at any stage of his trial apply to the court to amend or to divide a count that (a) ... or (b) is double or multifarious, on the ground that, as framed, it embarrasses him in his defence"

