    IF `the answer of s 589` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No count that charges an indictable offence other than murder shall be joined in an indictment to a count that charges murder unless" (section 589 bars the joinder)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:12677 | 591 (1) Subject to section 589, any number of counts for any number of offences may be joined in the same indictment, but the counts shall be distinguished in the manner shown in Form 4.
