§ `Section 592 -- Accessories after the fact`

-- Whether the principal or any other party "has been indicted or convicted or is or is not amenable to justice" does not enter into the answer, so none of those facts is asked.
-- src:12699 | 592 Any one who is charged with being an accessory after the fact to any offence may be indicted, whether or not the principal or any other party to the offence has been indicted or convicted or is or is not amenable to justice.
@ref s 592 (src:12699-12699)
GIVEN `the person is charged with being an accessory after the fact to an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 592 the person may be indicted as an accessory after the fact` MEANS
    IF `the person is charged with being an accessory after the fact to an offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any one who is charged with being an accessory after the fact to any offence"

§ `Section 593 -- Trial of persons jointly`

-- The offences are named by section number (PLAN.md rule R1): section 354, section 355.4, paragraph 356(1)(b) (subsection written "(1)(b)").
-- src:12701 | 593 (1) Any number of persons may be charged in the same indictment with an offence under section 354 or 355.4 or paragraph 356(1)(b), even though
-- src:12702 | (a) the property was had in possession at different times; or
-- src:12703 | (b) the person by whom the property was obtained
-- src:12704 | (i) is not indicted with them, or
-- src:12705 | (ii) is not in custody or is not amenable to justice.
@ref s 593(1) (src:12701-12705)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 593(1) any number of persons may be charged in the same indictment with the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 354 OR `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 355.4 OR (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 356 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)(b)")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under section 354 or 355.4 or paragraph 356(1)(b)"

